\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces The Field Origin as a vortex core. \textbf  {Left:} A river whirlpool viewed from the side. Water spirals inward at the surface, passes through the vortex core, and disperses below. \textbf  {Right:} The dual tetrahedral field structure. TetA spacetime (purple, top) with apex-up orientation, the Field Origin (red, center) at the coupling point where $\tau _{\text  {prop}} = 0$, and TetB spacetime (blue, bottom) with apex-down orientation. Double-headed arrows indicate that the field propagates through each sector. The topology ensures continuity: angular momentum does not stop at the Field Origin but flows through it.}}{24}{figure.3}\protected@file@percent }
