\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {VII}{\ignorespaces Equations derived from $(3+1)^2$ topology with zero adjustable parameters. Every numerical factor emerges from $(3+1)$ recursion: prefactor $[(3+1)^2+1]/[3(3+1)+1]$, exponent $21 = 1 + (3+1) + (3+1)^2$, coupling $k^2 = (3+1)^2 = 16$, breadth $1 + 2k(k^2+1) + 1/[k(k+d)] = 137.036$. ${}^*$The Hubble constant prediction falls between the Planck~\cite  {planck2020} ($67.4 \pm 0.5$) and SH0ES~\cite  {riess2022} ($73.04 \pm 1.04$) measurements; percentage deviation is not reported because the observational range spans $\sim $8\%. Mean deviation of the remaining four quantities: $0.16\% \pm 0.07\%$ (standard error).}}{73}{table.7}\protected@file@percent }
